s":"discovered","validation_status":"pending"},"changed_fields":["progress.status","progress.extraction_status","progress.paper_card_status","progress.branch_update_status","progress.validation_status","paper-card","language-units","model-units","learning-audit","observations","extraction.visual_review","type-branch.A.rules","type-branch.A.rule-impact-report"],"event_hash":"e6df12855ad6a19c38f0fc6b1b45973ba3205d92291f3c77a80f98372c92b403","event_id":"TX-000094-0e29dfa83a21","event_type":"paper-closed","history_completeness":"native","paper_id":"P-A-2019-1902727-2e04a61b","previous_event_hash":"60c2bd8392a086b884661cacc60623d54a54b523aa101365f8dbe876ed793079","sequence":94,"timestamp_utc":"2026-07-15T15:28:26Z","type_branch_diff":{"new_language_unit_count":204,"new_model_count":11,"new_observation_count":382,"new_rule_impact_count":13,"problem_type":"A","section_contracts_after":17,"section_contracts_before":0,"shared_catalog_changes":[]},"unresolved_added":["The official task explicitly invites flight, fire breathing, trauma resistance, and climate effects, but the energy model includes only a human-reference maintenance proxy plus body growth; it omits flight, fire, thermoregulation, reproduction, and activity.","Climate affects only forage yield in the paper; no climate-to-dragon metabolism, water, shelter, prey physiology, migration cost, or seasonal availability path is modeled.","The official task requests community support at varying assistance levels, but c_i is never supplied and only Level 5 receives a numerical area and biomass result.","Equation 1 prints r(w)=r(1-w/w_m), while the preceding closure and Equation 2 require r_0(1-w/w_m); the coefficient symbol silently changes.","The prose says r_0, w_0, and w_m are all unknown even though w_0=10 kg is already fixed; no fitting system, residual, or parameter uncertainty is shown.","The 14,000 kg age-three anchor is not part of the official prompt and is not source-linked in the model section, yet it drives the asymptotic 1.481 million kg result.","The paper says the dragon reaches its maximum at age eight, but a logistic curve approaches w_m asymptotically; an explicit maturity tolerance is absent.","Figure 1 places an unattributed decorative dragon silhouette over the data curve even though the official problem warns against unauthorized images; it also occludes part of the analytical trace.","Equation 5 is presented as an American Sports Medicine Association formula, but reference [3] is a physical-activity/BMR paper and the exact coefficient source is not established.","The symbol w_0 denotes dragon birth mass in Equations 2-3 but human reference mass in Equations 5-6, creating an unresolved cross-model symbol collision.","The paper's own reference [2] is a re-examination of the three-quarter metabolic law, yet no alternative exponent or extrapolation bound is tested for a 1.481 million kg fictional animal.","The assumed protein, fat, and carbohydrate fractions are 16%, 16%, and 1%, totaling only 33%; the remaining mass and its energy accounting are not closed.","The assumptions page contains an incomplete body-composition sentence ending at 'the proportion ... to 16', so its intended percentages cannot be recovered from that declaration alone.","Equation 9 treats food energy as perfectly converted to body macronutrients and maintenance without digestion, assimilation, excretion, hunting waste, or prey-processing efficiency.","The sheep-demography assumptions give 0.107% births and 0.044% natural deaths per day, a 0.063% net rate, while the calculation later uses 0.0567 with no reconciliation.","The reported 16.4 years follows only if b-d is about 0.0567% per day; taking the printed b-d=0.0567 literally gives roughly 60 days, so percent and time units are missing.","Equation 12 is typeset as G=s_m/e^(b-d)-1 without a denominator bar or parentheses; Equation 11 implies G=s_m/(e^(b-d)-1), which is retained only as an intended reconstruction.","Equation 15 likewise lacks clear parentheses around both numerator and denominator; the 16.4-year result assumes T=(ln G-ln g_0)/(b-d).","The pre-stocking flock follows unbounded exponential growth with no forage, land, density, disease, sex/age structure, or carrying-capacity constraint, even though the next section sizes the pasture needed to sustain it.","Section 4.3.2 reports G=296,297 and 533,335 kg/day forage, while section 4.3.3 reports G=266,609 and 479,896 kg/day; both claim to inherit the same 4.3.1 output.","The text says the regional annual-yield equations appear in Table 1, but no Table 1 is present anywhere in the 24-page PDF.","The three representative datasets remain literal 'xx grassland' placeholders in prose, while Figure 5 later names Egypt, Australia, and Iceland; the source-to-region mapping is not documented.","Equation 19 exactly repeats Equation 16 despite the sentence promising a deformation at m=5; the explicit expanded regional equation is missing.","Table 2 appears to leave the arid-temperature coefficient cell blank and supplies only partial basis expressions, preventing a complete three-region, three-driver reconstruction.","No raw monthly forage/weather data, normalization ledger, coefficient file, stepwise selection path, residuals, fit metric, collinearity check, or code is provided.","Using the paper's downstream G=266,609 sheep gives annual forage demand about 1.7518e8 kg; dividing by Table 3 yields produces about 5293, 4090, and 8309 hm^2, not 3738, 2383, and 4843 hm^2.","Figure 6 is described as the land-area trend during continuous sheep expansion, but it contains only three static maximum-area squares and a track-field reference with no time axis.","The nested smaller squares and the '100 Standard Olympic Track Field' panel in Figure 6 are not defined, so their geometry cannot be interpreted or reproduced.","Assistance level is asserted to increase with species richness, but Table 4 supplies only an ordinal rank and average total biomass; neither quantity establishes animal calories available per area and day.","The Level 5 biomass arithmetic is reproducible, but the paper generalizes Fi to seven levels without the six missing c_i values, trophic composition, regeneration rates, or sustainable-harvest constraints.","Equation 22 calls b and d annual rates while the recurrence output is days; no annual-to-daily conversion is applied.","With Q0=20,000, K=200, and the printed positive b-d=23%, Q(t+1)=e^0.23 Q(t)-200 grows from the first step and never reaches zero, so the claimed 103-day extinction is impossible under its own recurrence.","The 103-day claim is close to the no-birth calculation 20,000/200=100 days, suggesting the stated growth term was effectively ignored without disclosure.","Equation 24's NPP arithmetic is 1.75e10 g/year, while the Summary reports 1.75e7 per year without a unit; only conversion to 1.75e7 kg/year reconciles the magnitudes.","The paper assumes dragon feeding and fire convert 25 km^2 of temperate evergreen forest directly to temperate grassland without a disturbance, severity, recovery, or transition-time model.","Figure 7's right panel appears to show body mass on a 1.8e6 scale but is labeled Daily Intake (kcal), so the output identity and unit conflict with the caption.","Tables 6-7 contain asymmetric and nonmonotone deviations: nominally larger positive or negative one-year-mass offsets do not consistently yield larger deviations, and even the age-one response does not match the imposed offset; no refit ledger is supplied.","A one-factor deterministic anchor sweep is labeled Reliability verification and used to trust the full environmental-interaction chain, but it does not test model form, climate regression, trophic assumptions, or external predictions.","The Strengths section claims a comparison with prehistoric pterosaurs, but no such calculation, data, or visual appears in the model body.","The third Weakness bullet is textually corrupted by an unrelated sentence about coefficient independence and repeated calculation, obscuring the intended limitation and repair.","The letter states daily consumption is 6e6 kcal, whereas Equation 7 approaches about 4.87e6 kcal/day; no rounding or alternate activity scenario explains the difference.","The letter says about 4800 hm^2 is needed to keep a dragon in the arctic, while Table 3's 4843 hm^2 result is explicitly built for three dragons.","The letter claims a city of three million people can support a dragon and invokes cattle-to-population and medieval productivity ratios that are absent from the body models, tables, and references.","Several climate and ecosystem inputs rely on generic Wikipedia/NationMaster URLs, no raw dataset is archived, and references [11]-[16] have malformed or mismatched citation formatting, weakening provenance.","No code, appendix, fitted parameter file, monthly observations, regression outputs, random seed, or machine-readable result ledger is supplied, so the full chain cannot be reproduced.","Direct evaluation of Equation 4 gives about 10.03 kg at age 0, 112.45 kg at age 1, and 14,003.84 kg at age 3; it does not pass through the claimed 35 kg one-year fitting anchor.","Using Equations 4, 7, and 9 at age 8 gives u(8) about 4.871e6 kcal/day and Equation 10 gives about 47.99 sheep/day, not the reported 56; 56 sheep would require 5.684e6 kcal/day."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 24 physical pages passed text, rendered-pixel, and complete visual-review checks; three contact sheets, Equations 1-24, Figures 1-7, Tables 2-7, the two-page stakeholder letter, and references were inspected.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"Two hundred four positive units implement 68 source-grounded action classes across 17 quantitative layouts; Summary has eight visual paragraphs, Introduction has two, and the third saturation pass added zero actions.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"Eleven model units, 14 dependency edges, and 24 visually checked numbered equations retain the growth, metabolism, intake, prey conversion, flock equilibrium, forage regression, community, impact, and sensitivity chains.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_model_units.py"},{"details":"The language-first audit passed with 17 five-part contracts, eight main argument chains, exact model/equation and visual retention, 204 positive dispositions, and 47 warnings isolated to G7.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_learning_audit.py"},{"details":"Paper card, 382 observations, 17 important visuals, complete extraction, language, models, audit, and 13 live A-rule impacts cross-validated against 41 A rules.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_paper_artifacts.py"},{"details":"Thirteen declared A-rule impacts appended only nominated evidence, preserved rule lifecycle, and produced staged/live byte-identical rules and impact-report files.","status":"pass","validator":"apply_rule_impacts.py"},{"details":"All 114 regression tests passed against the final live bytes.","status":"pass","validator":"python -m unittest discover -s tests -v"},{"details":"The authoritative G0-G8 language-first order and prospective/live transaction protocol remain valid.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_plan_protocol.py"}]}
