s":"discovered","validation_status":"pending"},"changed_fields":["progress.status","progress.extraction_status","progress.paper_card_status","progress.branch_update_status","progress.validation_status","paper-card","language-units","model-units","learning-audit","observations","extraction.visual_review","type-branch.A.rules","type-branch.A.rule-impact-report"],"event_hash":"799a284e98e15b3eab92301850751d10086e0ca770a81670109f68261ea9ecea","event_id":"TX-000097-37599409351e","event_type":"paper-closed","history_completeness":"native","paper_id":"P-A-2019-1919022-f4c0fbb6","previous_event_hash":"b31b185be5de658274f14903b36dcec2356fa5d5a16142359377c85de9284ff2","sequence":97,"timestamp_utc":"2026-07-15T17:18:50Z","type_branch_diff":{"new_language_unit_count":294,"new_model_count":12,"new_observation_count":508,"new_rule_impact_count":16,"problem_type":"A","section_contracts_after":18,"section_contracts_before":0,"shared_catalog_changes":[]},"unresolved_added":["The Abstract reports an upper mass of 1.17e3 kg, while Equation 13, the letter, and Appendix C use about 1.17e5 or 1.2e5 kg; the summary is low by a factor of 100.","The Abstract calls 2.4e11 J/month adult energy intake, but at the 79.2 t state the appendix formula gives about 2.40e11 J/month expenditure and about 4.27e11 J/month gross intake after growth and K=0.5655.","The Abstract presents 1.8e7 m2 as a general minimum region for three dragons, but the value is the temperate-forest activity scope; the same code gives much larger desert and ice-sheet requirements.","The introduction claims the work provides insight into realistic ecological games, but no specific non-dragon real-world application, data case, or external validation is described as required by the official task.","Table 1 assigns q the unit J/(kg h), although Equation 1 uses q as whole-animal metabolic rate and Equation 2 separately defines the mass-specific rate q_hat.","The symbol q is reused in Section 4.2 as a geometric occupancy parameter after serving as metabolic rate in Section 3; the cross-model notation collision is not acknowledged.","Table 1 labels c_i without a unit even though it is a migration rate used with d_i in month^-1 dynamics.","Equation 8 introduces lambda without defining its unit or value; Appendix E silently sets it to 2e7, the same number used for food energy per kilogram.","Figure 1 states E_in AR = E_assimilate = E_expend + E_absorb and omits E_fire, while Equation 5 and the code treat fire as a separate energy term.","The symbol table defines M in kilograms, but the q0 regression is fitted with mass in grams; the displayed equations do not expose the required 1000^(3/4) conversion.","The plotted rest and action lines are printed with fixed slope -0.25, while Appendix B freely fits both slope and intercept; direct regression gives slopes about -0.2692 and -0.2645.","The 3 g hummingbird row appears in Appendix Table 7 but is excluded from both regression arrays without explanation.","Appendix B names the action fit handle rest_line and the rest fit handle action_line; the final legend happens to look correct, but the implementation names obscure the state mapping.","The action state combines flying, hunting, and other activity under one coefficient and no time schedule; the model cannot separately answer the official flight-energy question.","The fire coefficient 6.69e6 J/kg is described as an estimate but has no heat-capacity calculation, temperature target, efficiency, source, or uncertainty.","The proposed gland, flammable liquid, and electric-eel ignition mechanism is speculative narrative and is not connected to the reported fire-energy coefficient.","Table 3 mixes biological production, respiration, and individual assimilation percentages without a consistent trophic energy ledger.","K=0.5655 assumes every kilogram of food is roasted with the same fire cost and that fire energy scales exactly with ingested mass.","The paper writes an energy-driven mass ODE in Equation 8 but never solves it jointly; Section 3.4 switches to an independently calibrated VB growth curve.","The dragon density is printed as 1e3 kg/m2 rather than kg/m3, making Equations 10-13 dimensionally invalid as written.","Bone strength is set 20-69 percent above the three table values with no aggregation or biological transfer rationale.","The geometric relation cube_root(V)=10 sqrt(A) is asserted without anatomical evidence and effectively fixes a constant body-to-bone slenderness across all sizes.","The factor-25 daily-activity load condition has no derivation, citation, or sensitivity analysis.","The body-size bound considers only axial bone compression and omits buckling, bending, fatigue, flight loading, muscle power, heat dissipation, and circulation.","Reference [7] is titled that the VB equation should not be used to model age and size at maturity, yet the paper uses it without discussing that limitation.","Only hatch and one-year masses calibrate k after M_inf is fixed; no later narrative size observations, residuals, or alternate growth-family comparison are used.","The stated fastest-growth band of 30-80 years is broad; the retained formula has a single derivative maximum near 527 months or 43.9 years, but that calculation is not shown.","Figure 3's colorbar encodes growth rate without a labeled unit, and its values are not tied to the claimed 30-80 year band.","Using Table 3's own ranges, primary-consumer NAR=(1-respiration)AR is about 0.28-0.40, not the asserted approximately 20 percent.","Equation 16 equates energy to NPP mass density times area and NAR, omitting the stated 1.8e7 J/kg conversion, grams-to-kilograms conversion, and years-to-months conversion.","Section 4.1 first says s supports three dragons, Section 4.3 calls s a dragon's minimum area, and Appendix E applies an additional factor of three; the entity level is inconsistent.","Appendix E hides multiple physical conversions inside the unexplained constant 33930, so the displayed Equation 16 is not the implemented interface.","NPP is described as consumer mass although net primary productivity is producer biomass; trophic roles are mislabeled at the model boundary.","Equation 17 prints c_i in the displacement sum, while Appendix D uses c(j); the governing equation and code implement different competitive interactions.","Initial occupied area is treated as competitive strength without ecological justification, so rank is inferred from the state it later predicts.","The geometric initial occupancies and migration rates are not checked for total occupancy, parameter admissibility, or empirical fit.","The activity scope S=5s is unsupported and is never varied even though it drives every ecosystem impact result.","The model equates the entire dragon activity scope with destroyed habitat, rather than representing predation, fire, water use, waste, competition, or partial habitat use.","Three dragons are represented by multiplying area rather than modeling overlapping territories, different ages, or separate movement paths.","D2 is called a destroyed-habitat ratio, but Equation 22 adds it back as repaired habitat; the symbol's stated meaning and algebraic role have opposite directions.","Equation 22 is described as a first-order linear differential system, but products p_i p_j make it nonlinear and S(t) makes it nonautonomous.","The repair fraction and lag have no empirical source, cost, labor requirement, capacity bound, or connection to community size.","eta is named a reduction ratio but equals remaining total occupancy divided by baseline; larger eta means less reduction.","xi is also named a reduction ratio but equals the fraction of population types that remain.","Appendix D counts states below 1e-4 and outputs count/max_i, which is an extinction fraction, the complement of the xi reported in figure captions.","The extinction threshold p_i<1e-4 appears only in code and is not justified or tested for sensitivity.","Table 6 labels the population-count column i even though its values 60, 30, and 15 represent n; units and sources for the parameter ledger are absent.","The 12.9 t and 79.2 t result states correspond to about 300 and 1000 months under the VB curve, but the text calls them young and adult without giving ages.","At the 79.2 t state, intake is about 1.78 times expenditure under K=0.5655, not only slightly larger as claimed.","The reported 5.9e6 m2 forest value is the paper's S=5s activity scope, not the minimum food-support area s, yet it is described as the minimum region.","The highlighted 1.8e7 m2 three-dragon value applies to the temperate forest only; the same appendix formulas give about 3.24e8 m2 in desert and 1.50e10 m2 on ice.","The text says desert area is ten times the forest value, but its own NPP and rest-fraction parameters imply about 18.2 times for the adult state.","The three-panel description calls both the first and third panels the left one; the third panel is energy expenditure.","Captions report xi at 12,000 months, while the body sometimes calls the right-hand eta curve the reduction ratio of population types, mixing the two metrics.","The claim that dominant populations are more affected than vulnerable populations is observed from selected trajectories but not derived from the model or tested across parameters.","The desert discussion calls the first 2,000 units years, but all equations and plot axes use months.","The ice-sheet discussion says eta of population types is zero; population-type survival is xi, while eta measures total occupancy.","Equation 23 replaces the death symbol d_i with undefined m_i and does not reconcile its summation with Equation 17.","D1>=1-m_i/c_i ignores the equilibrium occupancy terms that also determine extinction, so it is not the general exact threshold claimed.","The Odd-even Symmetry Law repeats the same odd-extinction/even-rank sentence twice and never states the even-extinction case.","The Odd-even claim cites an empty 'Figure .' reference and has no dedicated figure, derivation, table, or counterexample test.","The prose says Figure 15 is the no-reconstruction baseline, but the baseline is Figure 14; Figure 15 already uses mu=0.4.","Figure 17 with a 600-month lag shows strong oscillations and eta falling near 0.45 before partial recovery, yet the analysis reports only the endpoint and calls recovery faster or better.","Monitoring, reintroduction, soil repair, and feeding recommendations are not mapped to separate controls or costs; all are rhetorically compressed into mu.","The official requirement for community size under varying assistance is not answered: no assistance-level parameter maps feeding, labor, population, or infrastructure to dragon needs.","The strengths claim real-world transferability because parameters are adjustable, but no parameter identification or external case demonstrates transfer.","The limitations list only computational scale and seasonality, omitting the paper's major dimensional, calibration, coupling, and reproducibility gaps.","The letter says an adult dragon must eat 480 sheep weighing 25 kg but gives no time basis; 480 sheep provide 2.4e11 J gross, which is only the reported expenditure, not required gross intake.","Using the paper's own K and adult growth state requires about 21,347 kg or 854 25-kg sheep per month, not 480, before uncertainty in prey energy or waste.","The letter presents the 1.8e7 m2 forest result as a universal three-dragon minimum and omits the much larger desert and ice-sheet results.","The letter claims a wider dragon activity range causes less ecological damage; the model only reduces proportional damage D1=S/S0 when total region S0 grows, not total disturbed area.","The letter gives no community-size result, assistance-level comparison, quantified restoration cost, or warm-temperate/arid/arctic resource table.","In weightFigure.m the function handles m_t and dm_dt are printed as commented lines, but the script later calls them; the published code cannot run as shown.","evalPopulationChange.m prints func_d=@(t)... as a literal placeholder, so the population figures cannot be reproduced from the appendix.","The printed population driver fixes max_i=15, pp=0.003, alpha_r=0.3, and q=0.3, covering only the ice-sheet example rather than all forest, desert, and restoration figures.","calcDragonSpaceAndEnergy.m prints every func_d and energy function handle as @(t)... placeholders, so Figure 4 is not reproducible from the published code."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 32 physical pages passed text and rendered-pixel checks; all page texts, four contact sheets, four detail sheets, key original-resolution pages, and the official 2019 problem were read or inspected.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"Two hundred ninety-four positive units realize 98 source-grounded action classes in three granularities across 18 quantitative layouts; the third saturation pass added zero actions.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"Twelve model units, 17 dependency edges, and 35 visually checked formula interfaces preserve allometry, energy, growth, area, occupancy, restoration, metrics, thresholds, and implementation handoffs.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_model_units.py"},{"details":"The language-first audit passed with 18 five-part contracts, 12 main argument chains, exact model/equation and visual retention, 294 positive dispositions, and 76 warnings isolated to G7.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_learning_audit.py"},{"details":"Paper card, 508 observations, 12 important visuals, complete extraction, language, models, audit, and 16 live A-rule impacts cross-validated against 41 A rules.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_paper_artifacts.py"},{"details":"Sixteen declared A-rule impacts appended nominated evidence, preserved lifecycle state, and produced staged/live byte-identical rules and impact-report files.","status":"pass","validator":"apply_rule_impacts.py"},{"details":"All 114 regression tests passed against the final live bytes.","status":"pass","validator":"python -m unittest discover -s tests -v"},{"details":"The authoritative G0-G8 language-first order and prospective/live transaction protocol remain valid.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_plan_protocol.py"},{"details":"An independent reviewer reread all 32 pages, the official problem, all contact/detail sheets, and key rendered pages; it edited no files and its reliable corrections were integrated before freeze.","status":"pass","validator":"independent read-only formula and visual review"}]}
