overed","validation_status":"pending"},"changed_fields":["progress.status","progress.extraction_status","progress.paper_card_status","progress.branch_update_status","progress.validation_status","paper-card","language-units","model-units","learning-audit","observations","extraction.visual_review","type-branch.A.rules","type-branch.A.rule-impact-report"],"event_hash":"0afa7213db70f3945cde2235b36e03c56c31e021578721f1c8ab521b2248c215","event_id":"TX-000099-e31d723d2274","event_type":"paper-closed","history_completeness":"native","paper_id":"P-A-2019-1926690-fc36d223","previous_event_hash":"4f785ef169867a6b2330a2736532b4652f60b3d2f91e47159ee12adcba01096d","sequence":99,"timestamp_utc":"2026-07-15T19:02:00Z","type_branch_diff":{"new_language_unit_count":369,"new_model_count":15,"new_observation_count":599,"new_rule_impact_count":11,"problem_type":"A","section_contracts_after":16,"section_contracts_before":0,"shared_catalog_changes":[]},"unresolved_added":["The suitability expression is an equal average, although the prose calls it a weighted sum and publishes no weights.","The five normalized factors have no complete unit and normalization ledger, so the score cannot be independently reproduced.","Forty-five cells are said to be traversable in a day, but no area, distance, geometry, or adjacency matrix is reported.","Random region inputs are not accompanied by distributions, random seeds, repeated runs, or calibration observations.","The seasonal-temperature notation does not unambiguously identify the two uniform draws or their dependence.","No hemisphere mapping or season-transition process explains how S changes through the year.","The 50 degree cap is imposed without a lower cap, validation distribution, or temporal autocorrelation.","One passage says the initial dragons are no older than one year, while another initializes ages from one to four years.","The initial state omits sex, energy reserve, injury, lineage, and uncertainty despite later reproduction and health claims.","The model continues mining after a den has been found; Appendix A admits stopping is more realistic but would increase population.","Gold has no physical unit, depletion law, replenishment process, or independent validation.","Mining costs health, but the health scale, cap, mortality boundary, and energy interpretation are not defined.","A 50 percent independent daily den-find probability is assumed without evidence or den-capacity accounting.","The reptile allometric relation is extrapolated to dragon masses without uncertainty or a documented unit conversion.","Metabolism excludes flight, fire, hunting, migration, reproduction, trauma, thermoregulation, and recovery.","The ABM prey calorie rating runs from 0 to 10, but the hunting conversion assumes 5,000 calories per prey with no bridge.","Taking a ceiling forces at least one prey-equivalent per day for every positive mass, distorting low-demand agents.","The prose says hunting removes one forest unit per prey while Table 2 says ten, leaving environmental damage ambiguous.","The 0.1 suitability trigger is chosen without calibration, sensitivity, or stated false-migration cost.","The migration sentence is truncated at the page boundary, so the actual destination-choice rule is not recoverable.","Migration has no distance, time, flight-energy, route-risk, or climate-transition cost.","A 25 percent daily reproduction probability corresponds to roughly 91 event opportunities per year and is justified only by clutch size.","Sexual reproduction lacks partner pairing and double-counting rules; asexual reproduction lacks a calibrated biological rate.","Health increases by 15 daily without a stated upper bound, making long-lived agents accumulate an unphysical reserve.","Activity costs, forest costs, and prose descriptions are not reconciled into one executable ledger.","Fixed fullness-bin changes of 0.25 or 0.5 kg/day are not calibrated to the official one-year mass anchor.","The ABM weight transition is structurally incompatible with the regional food-modulated logistic ODE.","The intervention threshold has no unit or baseline maximum, so Table 3 cannot be replicated from the prose.","The 100-day outcomes are single stochastic runs: threshold 50 gives 2 dragons, 100 gives 0, 200 gives 39, 400 gives 42, and 1000 gives 40.","Restoration has no workforce, cost, production, land, or assistance-level state and therefore is not a community-size model.","Removing at most one dragon and restoring forest are asserted management capabilities without feasibility constraints.","Food availability enters both the realized growth coefficient and the separate supply-demand factor, creating double counting.","The multiplicative food ratio can reverse growth, but its units and mapping to prey dynamics are not derived.","The realized growth coefficient treats food intake as both a rate modifier and a later growth-sign modifier.","The regional metabolism coefficient and exponent are not accompanied by a fully reproducible source-unit conversion.","Food eaten is proportional to prey count and dragon mass without region area, prey density, handling time, or saturation.","The final visually checked factor is c p/w^b, not its reciprocal; the paper does not establish its dimensional closure.","At w=w_max the logistic factor is zero, so an adult at the cap cannot lose mass even when food collapses.","With w_0=10 kg and w_max=6000 kg, the ODE no longer enforces the official one-year 250 kg anchor.","The linear rise from e_0=0.1 to e_max=0.5 at age 21 is selected without hunting observations.","The efficiency law omits learning variation, senescence, injury, prey defense, habitat, and season.","The prey equation has exponential growth and no carrying capacity, contradicting the claimed stable pre-entry ecosystem.","When the dragon is mature, the prey sign is controlled by j-e_max=0.25-0.5<0, so decline is built into parameter choice.","Prey count is continuous and can become negative under explicit Euler without a nonnegativity event.","The predation term is not reconciled with the energy intake used in the dragon growth equation.","Vegetation is defined as a proportion but plotted near 2, 7, and 40, outside the physical interval [0,1].","The vegetation equation has exponential growth and no carrying capacity despite the stable-baseline assumption.","At mature mass, l-g=0.09-0.2<0, so vegetation extinction is largely predetermined by coefficient signs.","The vegetation state omits deer grazing, climate, area, biomass units, and restoration feedback.","The e_max transition occurs near j=0.25 because the prey per-capita sign changes there; this is a structural identity, not external validation.","The g transition occurs near l=0.09 because the vegetation per-capita sign changes there; calling it a bifurcation overstates the evidence.","No positive coexistence equilibrium, Jacobian, stability domain, or uncertainty interval is established.","Forward Euler uses a one-month step without a time-unit reconciliation against derivatives stated per year.","No step-halving or convergence test shows that the dragon trajectory is numerically stable.","No positivity projection or event prevents deer population from crossing below zero.","No bounded-state treatment prevents vegetation proportion from exceeding one or becoming negative.","One-at-a-time sweeps omit parameter interactions, joint uncertainty, stochastic replication, and decision-reversal frequency.","The letter labels 2,647 deer/year as the full-grown requirement, but that value corresponds to a 12-year mass; Table 4 reports 2,666 for the full-grown case.","For a 250 kg cap, Table 4 reports a minimum of 158 and maximum of 2,627 deer/year without reconciling those regimes to welfare or control.","The prose says different initial weights are compared, while the table header varies maximum weight.","Maximum feeding outputs are described as observed feeding in the wild even though they are model-generated.","The 58 square miles is a one-year stock division, and the paper concedes no deer remain for the next year; it is not sustainable area.","The letter's 58-square-mile figure is for one annual deer stock, not a three-dragon land requirement.","The zoo table compares food quantities but never computes community population, labor, productivity, infrastructure, or assistance scenarios.","Reference [6] is a human cannibalism calorific-content paper rather than direct deer calorimetry.","The conclusion recommends captivity without an explicit optimization over ecological risk, welfare, cost, and support capacity.","Recipe pages use several images without source attribution, raising the official unauthorized-image concern.","The letter's climate advice is mainly qualitative and lacks consistent arid, warm-temperate, and arctic numerical resource comparisons.","The required community size under different levels of assistance is never modeled.","Real-world applications are named, but mechanism match and calibration to whale sharks, deer management, or wildlife ABMs are not demonstrated.","Independent range evaluation gives tropical winter temperatures down to -8 degrees C and arctic/tropical summer ranges up to 16/50 degrees C; no climate data validate these distributions.","The symbol T is reused for both the temperature function and the suitability normalization maximum, obscuring the interface.","The paper alternately describes three full-grown, mature, no-older-than-one-year, and one-to-four-year initial dragons with masses of 30-100 kg.","The prey rating increments daily and is deleted above ten, but the method never supplies a reproducible prey reproduction transition.","Even a starving juvenile gains 0.25 kg/day, so a 10 kg hatchling reaches at least 101.25 kg in one year, contradicting the official 30-40 kg anchor.","The paper says strict biological guidelines are conserved, but the ABM fixed mass bins and regional logistic ODE use incompatible growth and prey-energy mechanisms.","Because Equation (1) also has an outer factor p, dw/dt approaches zero as prey approaches zero; starvation freezes mass instead of producing loss or death.","A monthly-Euler reconstruction gives w about 5998 kg and p about 3 at 50 years, yet actual hunting is only about 1.75 deer/year against roughly 2668 deer/year metabolic need.","The Table 4 maximum deer counts do not match the declared one-month Euler scheme and are closer to a hidden fine-step or continuous calculation.","At 6000 kg the formula gives about 2668.7 deer/year; the table's 2666 is closer to the not-yet-full 15-year mass around 5992.6 kg.","The 2647/45 calculation is 58.82 square miles and should round upward to at least 59; three one-year stocks require roughly 176-178 square miles before sustainability.","The conclusion calls the regional system one-predator/multiple-prey, but Equation (2) has only one aggregate deer state.","Climate recommendations shift among semi-arid, tropical, wetter temperate, and tropical-to-semi-arid preferences without a controlled migration comparison.","The conclusion presents sea-ice melting as general even though Appendix A ranges from complete Antarctic loss to mild or no loss in fully frozen cells.","Temperature affects ABM suitability but not metabolism, energy demand, health, or the regional ODE, so climate-energy claims are disconnected.","Figure 9's caption states a transition between .05 and .01; the ordered interval and body discussion indicate .05 to .10.","Figure 8's legend includes an extra 1000 series and an irregular order that is not reconciled with the stated initial-prey scenarios."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 31 rendered pages passed extraction and complete visual-review checks; 31 nonempty text segments, four contact sheets, four detail sheets, and original-resolution formula/result pages were inspected.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"369 positive units implement 123 source-grounded language action classes across 16 quantitative chapter layouts; Abstract and Introduction preserve paragraph chains and the third saturation pass added zero moves.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"15 connected model units, 21 dependency edges, and 32 visually checked interfaces retain the ABM, ODE, numerical, and captivity chains.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_model_units.py"},{"details":"The language-first audit passed with 16 five-part contracts, exact model/equation and visual retention, 369 positive dispositions, and 87 warnings isolated to G7.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_learning_audit.py"},{"details":"Paper card, 599 observations, 23 important visuals, complete extraction, language, models, audit, and 11 staged/live A-rule impacts cross-validated.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_paper_artifacts.py"},{"details":"11 declared A-rule impacts appended only nominated evidence, preserved lifecycle, and produced staged/live byte-identical rules and impact-report files.","status":"pass","validator":"apply_rule_impacts.py"},{"details":"All 114 regression tests passed against the final workflow.","status":"pass","validator":"python -m unittest discover -s tests -v"},{"details":"The authoritative G0-G8 language-first order and prospective/live transaction protocol remain valid.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_plan_protocol.py"}]}
