itive normalized field is called a criminal-location probability although no generative likelihood, prior, or calibration test supports that interpretation.","Finer meshes are said to approximate an ideal smooth solution, but no resolution sensitivity or convergence diagnostic is shown.","The concrete 2 GHz runtime and 36 by 36 meter England-grid claim has no implementation, benchmark log, memory use, or kernel specification.","The prose says lower squared distribution deviation means a more likely next crime, but Programs 2 and 3 normalize the deviation without reversing its order, so larger deviations receive larger returned values.","The prose says virtual crimes are not added in the buffer, yet Programs 2 and 3 iterate candidate g over the augmented grid G prime rather than the interior G.","Program 2 specifies a 40 percent boundary buffer, whereas Figure 3 and Program 3 use 30 percent.","The O(n^4) next-crime complexity collapses a two-dimensional n by m grid to one symbol and does not state the effect of crime count or buffer size.","The claimed factor-N caching speedup and normalization-preserving combination are not derived or benchmarked.","Near-perfect parallel speedup equal to the number of cores ignores communication, memory bandwidth, scheduling, and aggregation overhead.","With observed times t_1 through t_(N-1), the mean of the N-2 observed intervals normally has denominator N-2, not the paper's N-1.","The time method is called linear regression, but the displayed rule is a one-step average-span extrapolation with no fitted regression line or residual analysis.","Parameters a, c, and d in the time-weighting function are undefined and no fit, units, or sensitivity analysis is reported.","Only one time-weight family is studied in depth and the synthetic correlated/uncorrelated experiment omits seeds, sample size, Poisson rate, parameter values, and repeated-run uncertainty.","The validation withholds only the most recent event from two main case datasets rather than using rolling origins, an external set, or repeated cross-validation.","Search Cost tie handling is described only as no preference within the same color, leaving exact rank treatment and color-bin effects unspecified.","Table 1 does not label Search Cost as percent versus fraction and does not state the distance units for Error Distance.","Kernel and time-weight choices are developed and evaluated on the same small case collection, creating tuning and selection optimism.","Time coupling generally worsens the reported values, but the paper offers no statistical test and initially attributes the behavior to bad luck.","The conclusion extrapolates Sutcliffe performance to larger datasets without evidence that more data, different offenders, or different geographies preserve accuracy.","Jack the Ripper dates are printed as 1988 in Appendix A but as 1888 in the preceding date table.","Panel (l) is titled Next Crime Location Probability but its caption calls it a Criminal Location plot.","The page headed Model Plots for Chester Turner actually repeats Sutcliffe coordinates, data, and captions, so the promised Turner visual comparison is absent.","The references contain suspicious pagination, misspellings, and inconsistent bibliographic formatting, limiting reproducibility."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"33/33 text pages and 33/33 rendered pages passed extraction checks; page-complete visual review is recorded as complete.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"234 language units cover all 20 declared chapters with quantitative layouts, reusable slots, variants, and boundaries.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"234/234 units passed with two unrelated original instantiations each and no full-clause source copying.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_anticopy.py"},{"details":"31 model and algorithm interfaces retain 22 visually reconciled equations plus i