quared value as about 90 percent correlation, conflating coefficient of determination and correlation.","The choice beta=ln(15)/mean interval has no behavioral derivation, fitted loss, external calibration, or sensitivity analysis.","Holdout prediction evaluates the center at the actual next-event time, information that would not be known at deployment.","The axis-wise mean-error diamond is not calibrated as a coverage region and has no stated probability interpretation.","The constrained utility optimization omits a Lagrange multiplier and incorrectly states partial U over partial p_i equals zero as the full first-order condition.","The implicit-function argument lacks the required non-singular Jacobian and explicit treatment of the simplex constraint.","Leaving utility and the choice functions arbitrary makes the general model weakly identified before the paper selects a kernel.","Binary prior-use risk forces an already used location to zero probability, an assumption violated by the DC Sniper sequence.","The kernel sets the exact anchor cell to zero and combines buffer and normalization terms without fully documenting their construction.","The product likelihood assumes a conditional generation structure that is neither estimated nor empirically checked.","The next-site double sum mixes multiple prefix states and anchor hypotheses without a clear normalization or forecast-time interpretation.","Several outputs are called probabilities although the implementation and evaluation mainly establish relative rankings.","Wikipedia, newspaper, and web addresses are used without a reproducible snapshot, geocoding log, or source-error assessment.","Berkowitz shooting sites and Hillside Strangler body-disposal sites represent different behavioral targets but are treated under one interface.","Physical page 11 contains consecutive headings '4 Data' and '5 Data', exposing an unresolved structural editing error.","Hit Score changes with hunting-area boundary and grid resolution, neither of which receives a sensitivity study.","The Yonkers hunting area is explicitly enlarged to include the known home, making that reported evaluation partly outcome-informed.","The chi-square goodness-of-fit comparison does not state samples, bins, degrees of freedom, dependence treatment, or implementation.","Three dependent case scores do not support the broad claim that the model is statistically superior to random search.","Next-event validation is dominated by qualitative single-holdout maps rather than repeated rolling-origin tests.","Jeopardy maps use blue, red, green, and purple categories without a continuous color bar or numeric probability scale.","The claim that error decreases after every added crime conflicts with Table 2, where the sixth-event error rises sharply.","The five Table 2 errors average about 15.15 km, not the 15.12 km stated in the discussion.","The Python simulation code and Excel macros are not supplied, preventing exact reproduction.","The Combined Models section displays outputs side by side but does not estimate or validate a fused decision rule.","The recommendation that police can fill population and geography gaps provides no formal adjustment protocol, calibration check, or safety rule."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"26/26 text pages and 26/26 rendered pages passed extraction checks; page-complete visual review is recorded as complete.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"224 language units cover all 18 declared protocol chapters with quantitative layouts, reusable slots, variants, and boundaries.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"224/224 units passed with two unrelated original instantiations each, no full-clause matches, and no source-fact leaks.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_anticopy.py"},{"details":"34 model and algorithm interfaces retain 25 visually reconciled equations plus inputs, conditions, calibrat