d and no construction for sixteen disks.","The description of the continuous disk-covering problem as simply unsolved and NP-complete needs a precise decision formulation and citation match.","Figure 3 appears to contain nineteen circles in a 3-4-5-4-3 arrangement while the text and caption claim twenty-one.","The hexagonal construction is an asserted feasible bound, not a proof that twenty-one is instance-optimal.","The inverse-fourth power relation is presented too generally; it is a two-ray far-field asymptote under specific conditions.","The uniform population generator is not specified; uniform radius sampling would bias points toward the center.","The spatial process is not classical Barabasi-Albert degree-proportional attachment despite using the name preferential attachment.","No displacement distribution, attachment radius, initial-user count, or random seed is reported.","Program 1 generates only initial users and then jumps to greedy graph coloring and frequency mapping.","Program 1 leaves total_users, r, and connect_chance unused and references undefined G and frequency_set.","The stated two-approximation requires a precise optimum k and applicability proof that the paper does not supply.","The basic O(s^4) derivation hides user count and candidate-evaluation data structures.","The probability that q independent repeaters all fail is p^q for one user, not n p^q; the latter can only resemble an expected count.","If layer utilities start at p, their geometric sum is p/(1-p), not 1/(1-p).","The downtime/utility parameter domain should be 0 <= u < 1 and the target ratio should satisfy 0 < W < 1.","Program 2 stops when current_utility/max_utility is below W, reversing the intended threshold logic.","Program 2 reuses u for downtime and candidate total utility, corrupting the subsequent user-utility update.","The optimized runtime claim lacks a precise update structure, memory cost, and proof.","The noncircular complexity ratio is undefined when min(a)=0 and is