violates the stated hard limit.","The printed 8.03 is truncated; ordinary two-decimal rounding gives 8.04.","Twenty-five residue classes do not all contain exactly Y/25 campsites unless Y is divisible by 25.","The orbit-spacing approximation uses 225/Y even though Y internal campsites between two endpoints imply Y+1 intervals.","The integer variables z_i lack a declared domain, solver, existence proof, and reproducible construction.","Filling positions ahead of a leader does not by itself prove optimality through startup, steady state, termination, and season boundaries.","Chart 3 uses six campsite nights for a seven-day type, exposing an unresolved days-versus-nights convention.","The formula m_i=floor(180 n_i/d_i) conflicts with route tables that occupy d_i-1 internal campsites and with the M-6 launch frequency.","Trip-count ratios do not equal orbit-size ratios when durations differ unless duration weights are retained.","Ignoring forgone loss supports an approximation, not an exact best-schedule proof.","The paper prints min A_i=A_3 although the retained seven-day oar type has the largest daily-hour requirement.","The paper prints A_i>=A_3 where the feasibility ordering requires A_i<=A_3.","The seven-point skeleton formulas do not specify rounding for noninteger fractions and contain a visibly malformed k range.","The threshold 306 sums durations, while the later Y=150 construction uses duration minus one; the campsite requirement is inconsistent.","The threshold 149 is arithmetically correct but adopts a different campsite-night convention from the 306 threshold.","Replacing 7,7,8 by arbitrary combinations does not prove daily travel or collision feasibility for every requested ratio.","The claim of uniform type distribution is contradicted by motorized six-day trips launching on both days of the cycle.","Twenty-five distinct feasible types produce twenty-six launches per two-day cycle because M-6 is duplicated; the prose risks conflating types and launches.","