count, boat ordering within each minute, simultaneous campsite arrival resolution, or closed-season censoring.","Figure 2's caption says percent of boats failing, but its vertical axis and data show campsite utilization.","Figures 2 and 3 repeat essentially the same slow-boat minimum-night utilization curve without explaining the duplication.","Several figure captions print Delta where the plot title uses Delta X, weakening symbol consistency.","The agent failure curve and the claimed seasonal capacity are not connected by a reproducible table, seed, repeated-run interval, or exact interpolation rule.","The 1170 seasonal-trip claim does not state whether it counts launches or completed trips and does not reconcile end-of-season boats still on the river.","The itinerary target formula uses L without defining it and hard-codes i=1,...,6 although the algorithm later evaluates seven or more daily rafts.","The itinerary algorithm sorts by boat speed but its boat-generation step explicitly samples duration only, leaving speed generation implicit.","Removing a boat after a greedy placement failure does not specify whether prior placements are rolled back or the schedule is recomputed.","The prose cites Figure 11 as campsite utilization versus campsite count, but Figure 11 is failed rafts; Figure 12 is the utilization plot.","The paper calls Delta X at least seven an overdrive even though seven is also its stated carrying-capacity boundary; strict overdrive would begin above seven.","The claim that utilization approaches 100 percent is based on a plotted plateau around 94 to 95 percent and no exact data table.","Figure 14 places the Delta X=7 failed-boat mean speed closer to 8 mph than the prose value of approximately 7.5 mph.","The probability model combines unconditional independent exponential increments with a fixed total stop count without explicitly conditioning the Poisson process.","The nightly uniform fleet argument requires steady state, equal stage representation, common support, independence, and ignored start/end transients that are not fully stated.","The text says K is Binomial(N-1,2), using 2 where a binomial success probability such as w is required.","The printed P(B) factor C(2,1)w(1-w) is not the conditional split probability of one boat in w and one in the adjacent D interval after conditioning on two boats in w+D.","The two displayed equal-speed events are not a complete general cutoff calculation unless delta's campsite interval, direction, occupancy, and all blocking configurations are fixed.","The mixed-speed formulas replace geometric threatening regions with p_f-scaled interval lengths without deriving the needed joint position, type, speed, and arrival-order probabilities.","The probability plots are described as travel of 14 miles without consistently distinguishing exactly 14, at least 14, and more than 14 miles.","A 1.25-mile spacing is not one hundredth of a 225-mile river and would imply roughly 180 intervals, not the printed 99 campsites.","The 77/12 times 180 calculation counts launches under a 180-day approximation and does not require those trips to finish within the season.","Agreement among the three models is not independent validation because they share river length, even campsite spacing, controlled demand assumptions, season horizon, and throughput ambiguities.","No executable code, seed, simulation configuration, raw output table, uncertainty analysis, or frozen source archive is provided.","The reference gives Ithica, NY for Cornell University; the place name is Ithaca."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"36/36 text pages and 36/36 rendered pages passed extraction checks; complete page-aware visual review is recorded.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"460 language units cover all 12 unique declared protocol chapters with quantitative layouts, reusable slots, variants, and boundaries.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_un