m that an empty site must eventually be found is not a complete termination proof and the lastSite=-1 boundary is not handled.","reschedule() deletes a boat's historical cells without rolling back or recomputing later boats whose placements depended on those cells.","Season-end calls to reschedule() do not increment lateTrips or the lateness statistics, so final nonfinishers are omitted from that metric.","addBoats() uses continue for requests that cannot finish before season end, permanently removing them from the queue rather than recording rejection or censoring.","Running thousands of random request orders and keeping the best is a best-observed heuristic, not a proof of an optimal pre-schedule.","The paper supplies no random seed, frozen configuration, raw run outputs, confidence interval, or uncertainty propagation for its reported averages.","The appendix main method performs one run, so it does not reproduce the stated ten data points with one thousand iterations per point.","m_C is measured in campsite indices, but the prose compares it with eight to fifteen percent of maximum travel distance without a consistent unit conversion.","The selected m_C=4 is not reconciled with the eight-to-fifteen-percent rule across campsite counts and craft types.","Magic and black-magic settings are inferred from floor jumps and simulation behavior; they are not a general optimality theorem.","M=182Y/Lbar is not rounded to an integer and therefore is a continuous reference, not a strict maximum count of complete trips.","Efficiency uses n times average trip length rather than exact occupied schedule cells even though the complete schedule exists.","For clipped Gaussian requests the authors acknowledge that the efficiency calculation is not accurate, yet compare it with the uniform case as if metrics were directly aligned.","Figure 4 labels its horizontal quantity as a ratio of motor boats to oar boats, but the 0-to-1 scale functions like a motor fraction.","The authors call high motor-share points inaccurate and provide no error bars, so the small fitted improvement is not securely resolved.","The reported 98.8 percent is utilization under synthetic demand and assumed geometry, not an empirical validation of river carrying capacity.","The statement that the best possible efficiency is around 99 percent is not derived as a formal bound.","The claim that river lengths from 25 to 257 miles differ by only about eleven trips lacks the complete scenario table and uncertainty needed to reproduce it.","Math.abs(Integer.MIN_VALUE) remains negative, so the uniform trip-length expression has a rare out-of-range failure path.","countCrossovers() is not tested or formally justified and its nested ordering logic may duplicate or omit crossover events.","Linear extraction damages smart punctuation, inequality signs, ceil and floor brackets, mean bars, and two-dimensional formula layout; rendered pages are required for fidelity.","The internal boat states and labels in Figures 1 and 2 do not enter text extraction and cannot be reconstructed from captions alone.","Reference 5 loses an underscore in extraction; the web references lack access dates and Reference 2 lacks a publication year.","The source contains grammar and spelling defects including where for were, procede, addBoats()which, and a double negative in the rollback proposal.","The phrase move back means retreat from a preferred downstream site, not physical upstream travel, and can be misread against the no-backwards assumption.","Trips, completed trips, rescheduled trips, schedule occupancy, and seasonal capacity are not kept as consistently distinct output types.","First-come individualized demand and best-of-random pre-scheduled demand are mixed when interpreting optimality and efficiency.","The greedy priority and displacement procedure is not shown to maximize completed trips globally or minimize crossovers globally.","No target-river occupancy, failure, environmental, ecological, safety, or demand data calibrate the operating recommendation.","MOVEMENT_CONSTANT is declared as 4 but getPreferredNextSite() hard-codes +4, so changing the named constant does not change behavior.","MOTOR_SPEED=80 and OAR_SPEED=40 are daily distance limits although getSpeed() and earlier prose use mph language; the unit naming is ambiguous.","The Gaussian harness clips values to seven and nineteen, creating endpoint probability masses rather than sampling a mathematically truncated Gaussian.","The test harness prints diagnostics without assertions or nonzero failure status and does not validate distribution or campsite input, so it is not an automated regression test."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"26/26 text pages and 26/26 rendered pages passed extraction checks; complete page-aware visual review is recorded.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"560 language units cover all 14 unique declared protocol chapters with quantitative layouts, reusable slots, variants, and boundaries.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"560/560 units passed with two unrelated original instantiations, no full-clause matches, and no source-fact leaks.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_anticopy.py"},{"details":"29 model and algorithm interfaces retain 8 visually reconciled equations plus inputs, conditions, handoffs, validation links, and limitations.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_model_units.py"},{"details":"14 five-part chapter contracts, the exact 6-paragraph Summary and 1-paragraph Introduction chains, positive organization artifacts, 11 visual dispositions, and 40 last-pass warnings passed.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_learning_audit.py"},{"details":"The paper card, 1128 observations, cumulative B rules, extraction, language/model records, and complete visual review cross-validate.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_paper_artifacts.py"},{"details":"12 nominat