lity.","The paper says the dynamic model can be planned in advance but does not specify the optimization horizon, forecast update, rollback, or computational complexity.","The bump coefficient beta and ideal movement y-star are displayed as the same ratio despite serving priority and movement roles.","The conflict step says cells with more than two visitors, apparently omitting the exactly-two case that should already violate one-group campsite capacity.","Bump direction reversal is mentioned, but tie handling, boundary handling, repeated collision resolution, and termination are not formalized.","Poisson loading lacks a seed, repeated-run count, warm-up, confidence interval, and explicit mapping from arrivals to individual trip requests.","The seven implementation variants do not report matched random streams or replication uncertainty, limiting causal claims from Tables 4 and 5.","The carrying-capacity definition uses fewer than ten interactions per person per day, while the final result reports interactions per person per season.","The source says one rafting reason where season is intended, and its encounter metric omits raft-to-camp and camp-to-camp measures defined earlier.","Table 5 implementation G duplicates the visitor and percentage pattern of Table 4 implementation D, which may be a copied row but is visually present in the source.","Tables 4 and 5 provide single point estimates without seeds, run counts, variance, intervals, or raw outputs.","Figure 5 alternates among interactions per tourist, per trip, per visitor, per person, per day, and per season without one invariant denominator.","The argument compares a ten-interactions-per-day standard with fewer than ten total interactions over a season, a dimensional mismatch.","The claim that off-schedule completion becomes independent of lambda at large Y is visual and has no fitted model, uncertainty band, or tested-domain boundary.","The result alternates between 1102 and 1102.8 without an explicit roundi