al overlap with bounded random is treated as no significant difference, although interval overlap is not the reported hypothesis test.","Equations 14 and 17 define C(u) as a dimensionless alternating integer while the route uses it as a physical stripe displacement. The visually printed formulas appear to omit a sight-range scale such as d.","Equation 15 does not make clear whether C(j) is an absolute vertical coordinate or an incremental displacement, nor whether j and epsilon update before or after the move. Preserve this ambiguity in any transcription.","Equation 18 adds scalar C(j)r to vector S_i, reuses r from lost-aircraft glide range, and flips epsilon although its downstream role is unclear. The printed transition is dimensionally and algorithmically incomplete.","The source rounds a cited 97-percent operator recognition probability to one, raising P(D_u) from about 0.776 to 0.8. Its minimum-90-second view claim assumes a full 20-mile diameter crossing and does not cover a marginal target encounter.","The Bayesian B777 interval is arithmetically inconsistent: 6.21463 plus or minus 2(0.246568) gives a lower bound about 5.72149, not 5.57215. The page also describes samples of size 100 although this run used 500 trials and 475 successes.","Uncertain-model means and intervals omit trials not found by 24 hours. Comparing Bayesian 95-percent completion with spiral 80-percent completion through success-conditional intervals does not compare overall time-to-discovery distributions; censoring or restricted-time analysis is required.","The C172 discovery probability is produced by linearly scaling rectangular aircraft size from the B777 to 2 percent. No evidence shows radar/debris detectability is proportional to that geometric area, and the reported SD/SE imply a sample count inconsistent with 411 successes.","The abstract attributes an average time of about 4.7 hours to the Bayesian method, while the body reports Bayesian mean 6.21463 hours; 4.76078 hours belongs to the uncertain spiral route. The recommendation must use route-labeled result records.","The paper dates MH370's departure as March 4, 2014 rather than March 8, and page 6 states that Amelia Earhart fragments were finally found although its cited context remains unresolved. These contextual facts require source verification before reuse.","Page 56 visibly ends the sentence 'Furthermore, the Bayesian Solution' before the recommendation, and page 61 labels image references as 8.2 after Section 10. These are genuine source organization/provenance defects rather than extraction clipping."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 61 physical pages have page-aware extracted text and a complete visual review. Byte-bounded JPEG review proxies covered every page, and focused crops reconciled formulas and small labels without transporting an original full-page PNG.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"64 language units cover all 16 protocol chapters with measured layouts, reusable slots, variants, boundaries, and zero-action saturation passes.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"64/64 units passed against the complete 61-page extracted source text with no failed original-instantiation checks.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_anticopy.py"},{"details":"11 model units retain 23 visually checked equations and 15 dependency edges plus variables, conditions, algorithms, handoffs, validation links, and limitations.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_model_units.py"},{"details":"16 five-part chapter contracts, 7 Abstract paragraphs, 4 Introduction paragraphs, 4 main arguments, 42 visual dispositions, and 15 last-pass warnings passed.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_learning_audit.py"},{"details":"The paper card, 334 observations, 23 cumulative B rules, extraction, language/model records, and complete visual review cross-validate.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_pap