ironmental investment per tourist, ruling out a potentially relevant policy regime.","dRetaliatoryKillings/dt=c*Predator-B*Tourism has no state-dependent damping and can produce negative retaliation values.","The A/Tourism term is singular at zero and no positivity or invariant-region proof is supplied.","Non-negativity, boundedness, and physical feasibility are not proved for all six state variables.","A damper of 25 is introduced after observing a roughly 150-unit cycle and is claimed not to affect behavior without a derivation or calibration record.","Many parameter values are described as slightly modified or subjectively estimated without a reproducible transformation ledger.","The Figure 2 discussion reverses the table's prey and predator units, calling predators hundred-thousands and prey thousands.","Table 1 labels equations 4.1-4.6 while the final displayed system is numbered 5.1-5.6.","The tourism approximation is set around 10 to fit an upward trend, but the observation, time unit, and fitting criterion are not documented.","The non-trivial equilibrium is written symbolically without explicit positivity conditions or a numerical coordinate table.","Asymptotic stability is asserted without listing the six numerical eigenvalues, precision, solver, or reproducible embedded code.","A three-variable projection is compared to a two-dimensional spiral sink without establishing that the plotted trajectory proves the full six-dimensional classification.","The text names eight controllable parameters, while the displayed policy vector has seven entries because Pt-It is combined.","The utility combines fauna, tourists, degradation, poaching, retaliation, and cost using arbitrary weights without normalization or a dimensional ledger.","The prose does not unambiguously list all six outcome weights in vector order, making the exact utility calculation hard to reproduce.","All policy parameters share one quadratic cost coefficient despite radically different units and implementation mechanisms; the authors acknowledge this flaw.","The displayed Table 4 cost entries sum to about KSh466.8 million, not the stated approximately KSh379 million.","The claimed 46 percent increase over fiscal-year 2019-2020 is not accompanied by a clearly frozen baseline budget calculation.","L-BFGS-B is named, but parameter bounds, initialization, convergence tolerances, gradients, and local-optimum checks are absent.","Optimization uses equilibrium outcomes and does not price transient harm, seasonal peaks, or the time required to reach equilibrium.","Concrete actions are mapped to abstract parameter changes without an estimated action-to-parameter response function.","The OAT analysis refers to each parameter's maximum range but does not list those ranges or the perturbation grid.","Sensitivity rechecks stability classification rather than the budget optimum, outcome magnitudes, or policy rank reversals.","The reported m<53.77 condition is not derived in the paper or connected to a physically plausible migration unit.","Generalization advice is qualitative; no destination reserve is recalibrated or externally validated.","The committee report recommends reducing all areas proportionally if funding falls, which conflicts with the preceding ranked priorities.","The committee report summarizes animal populations as about +25% although the technical result separately states +24% prey and +78% predators.","The appendix provides only an external 'Code is viewable here' link; no executable code, data snapshot, environment, or expected output is embedded."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 25 pages retain text, rendered pixels, complete visual review, 29 equation interfaces, seven figures, five tables, four other structures, and eight byte-bounded JPEG proxies.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"All physical pages were read in order with source wording, equations, tables, figures, references, and th