ter selection, and residual diagnostics are absent.","Figure 3 is interpreted visually without numerical held-out forecast metrics.","The normal random input is not linked to a fitted residual distribution or temporal and spatial correlation structure.","The uncertainty ratio is defined with absolute values while Figure 4 displays negative uncertainty values.","The paper shifts between maximum relative error and an average uncertainty of 2.39 percent without a fully specified aggregation convention.","The ridge penalty coefficient, feature basis, training set, cross-validation, and spatial-depth domain are not reported.","Only a few predicted samples are tabulated; regression error and held-out validation are absent.","Hydrodynamic resistance should depend on relative water-submersible velocity and direction, which the force model does not fully reconcile.","Equation 18 prints the same cosine resistance component in both horizontal equations, suggesting a sine-cosine transcription or model error.","Angle definitions, sign conventions, seabed and surface contact, and collision behavior are not fully defined.","The trajectory solver, software, step size, current interpolation, parameter values, and initial-condition construction are absent.","Coordinate signs and digits are corrupted in extracted text; exact trajectory values must be anchored to the source visual.","The three-hour point estimate has no propagated uncertainty band despite the preceding 2.39 percent current-forecast claim.","Communication ranges, depth ratings, costs, maintenance, readiness, compatibility, and product sources are not frozen.","Range divided by sensitivity is dimensionally and semantically unclear, and multiplying six raw coefficients produces an unnormalized score.","Table 6 averages products or models without preserving product-level provenance or uncertainty.","The maintenance-cost-over-usage term is not tied to a consistent annual or mission time basis.","The equipment decision is described as purchase yes-no in one place and as a quantity in another.","The readiness objective is actually preparation time, so lower values are better even though the prose sometimes treats readiness as a positive score.","Population, generations, bounds, crossover, mutation, seed, convergence, and repeated-run stability are absent.","The displayed front is nearly linear and is not accompanied by dominance, crowding, or robustness diagnostics.","Culling and rounding continuous genetic-algorithm outputs can destroy Pareto optimality, but the four integer schemes are not re-evaluated.","The final four schemes are chosen subjectively without a decision rule for host versus rescue vessels, capacity, budget, compatibility, or redundancy.","The recommended 1+n rescue arrangement leaves n undefined.","Equation 27 mixes vessel speed, search time, sweep width, turns, and overlap in a dimensionally unclear equality.","The 300 m by 300 m grid is not reconciled with sensor footprint, depth, bathymetry, topography, or track overlap.","A Poisson law over Manhattan-distance rings is ad hoc and lacks calibration, domain truncation, and normalization proof.","The rule lambda=m+ln(t/t0) is asserted from a probability-time ratio without derivation or calibration.","The update advances target uncertainty but does not explicitly couple rescue-vessel relocation with moving-target dynamics.","Searched cells are set permanently to zero even though a moving target can later enter them.","The prose describes the denominator using searched-grid probability even though a no-detection event requires remaining or unsearched probability mass.","Accumulated finding probability assumes perfect detection and omits sensor POD, false negatives, terrain, weather, and revisits.","The 5-hour and 50-hour results use one missing point and one parameter setting without confidence intervals or repeated scenarios.","Independent equal targets are summed without vessel-task assignment, collision avoidance, fa