ut the accumulated drift, reset interval, acoustic fixes, clock synchronization, and outage behavior are not quantified.","The IMU reference frame is described as fixed and not moving with the submersible, which conflicts with the usual body-mounted IMU frame and leaves coordinate transformations unclear.","The paper calls a lumped rigid-body force ODE Computational Fluid Dynamics without a fluid domain, mesh, boundary conditions, discretization, or CFD validation.","The inertia, Coriolis, damping, restoring, and environmental terms are named but their matrices, hydrodynamic coefficients, frames, signs, and units are never instantiated.","The current vector reuses u, theta, and phi without a clean distinction from vehicle speed, heading, elevation, coordinate frame, or measured current direction.","Equation (3) prints a d-squared thrust factor; conventional nondimensional propeller thrust uses a fourth-power diameter term, so dimensions and source convention require checking.","Equation (6) drops the earlier Coriolis, damping, restoring, gravity, and buoyancy structure and does not reconcile the reduced equation with neutral buoyancy or vertical failure cases.","A linear Kalman filter is adopted although the current force and vehicle dynamics are nonlinear; no linearization range, EKF/UKF comparison, observability analysis, or consistency test is given.","Zero-mean Gaussian, time-independent process and sensor errors are assumed without residual diagnostics, cross-correlation analysis, or empirical distributions.","The claim that deterministic Newtonian mechanics makes the model and IMU data a Markov chain does not establish the stated stochastic transition and observation assumptions.","The filter is said to continue smoothly after pruning sensor observations, but covariance growth, remaining measurements, initialization, bias drift, and failure detection are not shown.","Q and R are attributed to extensive empirical testing without the data set, loss function, parameter search, innovation statistics, holdout case, or exact replay procedure.","The MATLAB trajectory is described as expected but no observed path, synthetic truth definition, baseline, error table, parameter bundle, or uncertainty interval is supplied.","Figure 9 calls a blue simulated trajectory the bona fide path, which overstates the status of a model-generated reference trajectory.","The Summary says 14 indicators while Section 4.1 and Table 2 use 13 performance indicators for 14 devices.","The text says each row is standardized, although PCA normally standardizes each indicator column across devices; the actual preprocessing code is absent.","Cost, failure rate, workforce, energy consumption, availability, readiness, and performance measures are mixed without explicit benefit/cost orientation, units, transformations, or missing-value handling.","Table 3's top scores and the three explanatory bullets identify Teledyne BlueView, Edgetech, and Soil Machine Dynamics Quantum EV, while the preceding recommendation sentence names Perry Slingsby devices and Divex AUV-1000.","The memo repeats Perry Slingsby Multi-Beam, Perry Slingsby Side Scan Sonar, and Divex AUV-1000, contradicting Table 3, Figure 10, and the body descriptions.","Availability, maintenance, readiness, workforce, energy, and cost are scored without lifecycle horizon, quantities, compatibility, spares, training, failure recovery, mobilization, or budget constraints.","The 95-percent three-dimensional feasible zone lacks the chi-square threshold, explicit ellipsoid equation, coordinate projection, covariance example, and coverage calibration.","The x-y-z errors are declared independent while the exposition retains a general covariance matrix; the diagonal restriction and its empirical validity are not shown.","Supplementary Kalman filters and particle replacement are described like a particle filter, but weights, resampling, particle count, process model, and distinction from a standard Kalman filter are absent.","P(found|t)=1/alpha^t is called a cumulative distribution even though it generally decreases for alpha greater than one, may be unbounded for other alpha, and is not calibrated to search effort or detection.","The claim that prior negative searches are ineffective ignores detector probability, revisits, target motion, Bayesian filtering, and the prompt's explicit cumulative-search-results requirement.","Along-isobath motion is justified only for a uniform slope and conical beam, omitting terrain variation, overlap, turns, speed, altitude, occlusion, false negatives, route constraints, and multiple vessels.","Initial deployment is set to the last transmitted position rather than optimized from the predicted feasible zone, travel times, host position, equipment range, or multiple deployment assets.","The paper supplies heatmaps and qualitative route claims but no denominator-aware function of time, cumulative search history, probability of detection, false-negative rate, or validated finding-time distribution.","Caribbean currents and bathymetry are compared visually, but no sourced fields, recalibrated coefficients, equations, cases, validation, or quantitative performance comparison is provided.","The multi-submersible section is qualitative and alternates among submersibles, submarines, and drones without dynamic Voronoi updates, communication limits, assignments, collision proof, or rescue priority.","Neighboring vehicles are said to be immediately notified when one is beyond communication range, leaving the detection and notification channel logically unresolved.","The perturbation magnitudes for density, current force, propeller speed, and mass are not stated, so cosine-similarity changes and RMSE cannot be reproduced or compared.","RMSE is computed against an actual path that is not defined as observed or simulated, and no repeated-run uncertainty, confidence interval, or held-out data are supplied.","Figure 19's caption varies environmental-turbulence parameter alpha, whereas Table 4 discusses density, current force, propeller speed, and mass; the plotted cases are not reconciled with the table.","The strengths section says the Kalman filter maintains multiple trajectories, while a standard linear Kalman filter maintains one Gaussian state estimate and covariance.","Environmental data, product parameters, manufacturer records, image sources, transformations, and access dates are not frozen into an auditable input bundle.","No code, complete parameters, units, data files, software versions, random seed, runtime, expected outputs, or end-to-end replay command is provided.","The memo presents the model as comprehensive and suitable for approval without stating uncertainty intervals, unresolved method conflicts, budgets, owners, triggers, monitoring, escalation, or rollback.","Several grammar slips, duplicated words, inconsistent device names, and shifting technical nouns are human-source texture but require factual reconciliation before any operational reuse."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 25 pages retain text and rendered pixels; the complete visual review binds 12 central formula interfaces, 19 figures, four tables, seven other structures, and eight byte-bounded JPEG proxies.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"All physical pages were read in order and aligned to official 2024 Problem B; the task ladder, assumptions with justifications, CFD preparation and results, Kalman filtering, PCA simplification, feasible-zone construction, search procedure, transfer analysis, sensitivity analysis, and regulator memorandum are retained.","status":"pass","validator":"source_coverage_audit"},{"details":"464 source-anchored language units cover 14 normalized chapters and preserve the human First-Then-Next-Furthermore-Finally Summary ladder, premise-justification pairs, habitual transitions, information order, paragraph progression, voice, tense, modality, visu