d terms and intervention vectors lack a complete dimensional analysis.","ELA change is attributed to tourist pressure and tax-funded restoration without a causal identification design or separation from climate drivers.","Tourist arrivals are treated as a logistic population although visitors are flows, seasonality is strong, and carrying capacity K is not independently justified.","The hotel-tax ODE does not explicitly include tax rates, lodging prices, collection lags, cruise visitors, or non-tourism revenue.","Policy effects omega_H, omega_N, and omega_T are added directly to state derivatives without documented units or a reproducible policy-to-coefficient mapping.","The 2013 Blob observation is removed and remaining years interpolated, but the exclusion rule, interpolation method, sensitivity, and retained sample size are not fully documented.","Nonlinear least squares is named without complete input data, starting values, bounds, residual diagnostics, confidence intervals, or holdout validation.","Figures 3, 4, and 8 show fitted behavior, but visual agreement is not a substitute for residual, predictive, and out-of-sample checks.","Nine allocation arrays do not establish coverage or optimality of the five-dimensional allocation simplex.","Eight policy vectors and the selected [-3,3,4] code lack a fully auditable mapping from integers to implementable policy magnitudes.","Allocation shares are optimized without a clearly frozen total budget, feasibility constraints, legal restrictions, or implementation costs.","The paper proposes iterative policy feedback but does not specify observation intervals, triggers, controller stability, delay, or rollback.","Several evaluation indicators reuse N and T, creating potential double counting that AHP weights do not remove.","Benefit and cost indicators are mixed; direction, clipping, and bounds are not consistently documented.","Equation (7) contains visually unstable arrows, exponents, and mu subscripts; its exact algebr