"The symbol c denotes the speed of light in E=hc/lambda but later denotes effective exposed area, creating a consequential symbol collision.","The HTM uses constant irradiance and full effective exposure, omitting solar angle, weather, spectrum, attenuation, shadowing, rotation, and time variability.","The HTM text calls itself the Low Transmittance model even though the section heading and subsequent comparison identify it as HTM.","The Abstract uses a 1x1x2 cm prism while the HTM section uses 1x1x3 cm for the same 1.86 g and 1.26 g annual-loss example.","The linear HTM has no zero-mass stopping rule and can predict negative mass if extrapolated beyond depletion.","Mechanical degradation is dismissed from particle size and collision arguments without quantifying torque, wave action, abrasion, or fragmentation.","Floating behavior is inferred from density while currents, biofouling, water ingress, aggregation, and vertical mixing are excluded.","The UV source is a constant Pacific Northwest sea-level average rather than a measured North Pacific Gyre spectrum and time series.","The material contains no UV stabilizers and is fixed to medium-density polyethylene, limiting applicability to common products and aged debris.","Only surfaces perpendicular to UV are degraded, so orientation, diffuse radiation, refraction, reflection, and curved-surface illumination are omitted.","The model treats transmittance as a high-versus-very-low split rather than a measured depth- and wavelength-dependent optical field.","Fast forward cleavage and termination with very slow reverse reaction are asserted through Krxn>>1 without rate constants or sensitivity analysis.","The LTM neglects trapped air even though the representative object is a hollow post-consumer container, so the waterline geometry may change materially.","Vertical kinetic equilibrium is imposed without waves, drag, capillary effects, rotation, or transient immersion.","A hollow sphere with fixed thickness is a convenient geometry but does not represent the observed irregular, fragmented, and size-converging debris population.","The model updates radius through remaining mass while holding thickness and shell topology fixed and does not model cracks, holes, breakup, or complete disintegration.","The paper correctly says U requires site calibration, but no field measurement, uncertainty, seasonal profile, or attenuation calibration is supplied.","Appendix A lists U=1400 in the model/input row but uses U=90 in annual calculation rows; the output is therefore not tied to one frozen parameter value.","Appendix A labels water and plastic density with g/cm^2 rather than g/cm^3 and contains column/formula presentation that is difficult to reconcile unambiguously.","The LTM first-year loss and long-run curve are presented without an observed degradation series, laboratory benchmark, residual, error metric, or uncertainty interval.","Calling both model outputs reasonable is an internal plausibility judgment rather than validation against field or laboratory data.","The model does not reproduce the reported tendency of particles to converge around 3-5 mm and does not include debris below the surface down to 100 ft.","Polyethylene is only one polymer, so the conclusions do not transfer to mixed plastic composition without new bond, density, stabilizer, and optical parameters.","The ecological discussion links predicted fragment mass to ingestion through possible food-size similarity, but it has no exposure, dose-response, species, or population model.","Cruise-ship and land-source recommendations rely on cited waste shares and governance claims rather than outputs of the photodegradation models.","Education, monitoring, and regulation are recommended without costs, authority, compliance, equity, alternative interventions, or measurable decision thresholds.","The Conclusion claims accurate and realistic prediction even though no empirical validation, uncertainty analysis, sensitivity study, or independent replication is reported.","The paper provides equations and an appendix table but no executable spreadsheet, code, frozen input dataset, or end-to-end reproducibility package."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 11 physical pages retain nonempty source text and 200-DPI rasters; physical page 2 is title/contents furniture, physical page 10 begins References at line 13, and physical page 11 is Appendix A rather than positive prose.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"All pages were read in order, beginning with the Abstract and Introduction. Coverage retains the concrete pollution problem, polyethylene photolysis, transparent and low-transmittance regimes, buoyancy geometry, spreadsheet recurrence, comparison, limitations, impact handoff, conclusion, and Appendix A calculations.","status":"pass","validator":"source_coverage_audit"},{"details":"Human style is captured through environmental narrowing to a calculable particle, a concrete input-output contract, mechanism-first derivation, reason-plus-omission assumptions, a simple transparent baseline before coupled buoyancy geometry, explicit refusal to invent an uncalibrated irradiance value, common-output comparison, and a restrained impact handoff that distinguishes modeled fragments from policy evidence.","status":"pass","validator":"human_style_learning_audit"},{"details":"123 source-anchored language units cover 8 normalized positive chapters and record function, information order, slots, variants, boundaries, two unrelated examples, and anti-copy restrictions.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"123/123 language units passed against reviewed positive author prose with two unrelated original instantiations each, zero full-clause matches, zero unique eight-word shingle matches, zero source-fact leaks, and maximum shared content run two.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_anticopy.py"},{"details":"