count rate, price year, currency normalization, financing, insurance, degradation, or uncertainty.","Table 2 appears inconsistent with the stated annual maintenance inputs and 500,000-km fuel calculation; the arithmetic is not independently reconciled.","The 5% one-at-a-time sensitivity analysis is local and does not test interactions, distributions, scenario ranges, or sign errors.","A moving road fleet is idealized as a stationary ground-level point source with uniform wind, no deposition, and no terrain or chemistry.","The Gaussian formula uses fixed sigma values rather than distance- and stability-dependent dispersion parameters.","The mass-conservation integral is displayed without finite domain, source height, reflection term, or numerical implementation details.","The plume simulations use circle counts derived from normalized coefficients, but axes, time, emission rate, and mapping from coefficients to circles are not fully defined.","Power-station emissions are assigned to EVs as direct emissions without transmission losses, generation dispatch, regional mix, temporal charging, or lifecycle boundaries.","Scenario totals multiply fixed per-kilometer factors by vehicle count but omit distance traveled and therefore do not preserve the stated g/km units.","AP combines unlike pollutants through an unexplained normalization and weighting scheme.","The 1.15-billion vehicle estimate is extrapolated from a short table without uncertainty, fleet-class definition, or scenario year alignment.","Figures 5 and 6 are internal scenario charts, not observations; the conclusion overstates improvements in dispersion speed and affected area.","Noise and health sections use small cited tables and qualitative claims without exposure duration, population, charging-field measurement, or causal validation.","Battery toxicity is described qualitatively, but chemistry, collection rate, recycling pathway, dose, and lifecycle comparison are absent.","Bass-type diffusion is used without documenting the historical series, fitted parameter values, residuals, confidence intervals, or out-of-sample performance.","The text states m>0 where the model uses market capacity M, and the stated parameter constraints are not tied to estimation.","The inflection-point expression is poorly typeset and is not carried into any numerical check.","Norton substitution assumes irreversible switching, constant purchase rate, a fixed 2015 market entry, and attraction of new users without stress tests.","The forecast axes and units are not fully documented; claims for 2028, 2042, 2045, and 2060 are not benchmarked against held-out data.","The proposed genetic-algorithm repair is not implemented, tuned, or compared with the curve-fitting method.","The crude-saving calculation assumes every replaced vehicle consumes 1.5 tons of fuel annually and treats gasoline-plus-diesel yield as a direct conversion ratio.","The electricity calculation uses a fuel-consumption proxy for travel and does not propagate efficiency, charging loss, mileage distribution, or generation loss.","Coal results are printed as kilograms although fleet-scale electricity implies much larger units; this is a severe scale or unit error.","AHP pairwise judgments have no respondent, elicitation process, uncertainty interval, or sensitivity analysis.","The aggregate consistency formula and weights a_j are not defined clearly enough for independent replay from the paper alone.","AHP weights are treated as physical generation proportions even though the criteria mix preferences, impacts, safety, and development without capacity constraints.","The final allocation omits load shape, dispatchability, resource limits, grid reliability, capital cost, emissions lifecycle, regional feasibility, and policy authority."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 20 physical pages retain nonempty source text and 200-DPI rasters; page 1 is Contents, page 2 starts Introduction, no title/Abstract/Summar