ed to source-specific technical capacity.","The cubic population extrapolation is bounded to 2060, but the 0.002t motorization multiplier is ad hoc and uncalibrated.","The hybrid exclusion is explained, but the claim that hybrids are no better than gasoline cars is stronger than the supplied evidence.","The 90% electric-range statistic rests on one dated source and is not reconciled with heterogeneous travel demand.","E denotes both a proportion and a time-dependent vehicle count, creating a consequential notation ambiguity.","Breakdown probabilities are fixed from nominal eight- and twenty-year lifetimes and ignore age structure and survival distributions.","Purchase probability is set equal to current global electric share without behavioral calibration.","The coupled differential equations are not derived from a consistent stock-flow balance and may double-count growth or replacement.","Euler's method is named without step size, truncation error, stability analysis, or convergence evidence.","The need for a positive seed follows from the model's absorbing zero state and is not empirical proof that a subsidy is necessary.","Seeding cost ignores financing, discounting, purchase timing, administrative cost, and fiscal feasibility.","The local stay and switch probabilities and their 1/8 and 1/20 factors are asserted rather than estimated.","The 3/40 cellular update is not fully derived from the printed transition probabilities.","The snowball constant k=4 and 80% local influence are arbitrary and acknowledged to need observation.","The cellular automaton reports no grid size, boundary condition, random seed, replication count, or variance.","The claim that locality slows adoption comes from one internal simulation rather than an observed benchmark.","The 52.8-kWh charge is inferred from 110 V and eight hours without current or charging efficiency.","Nuclear and renewable footprints are called negligible without life-cycle system boundaries.","Pollution factors, geography, generation boundary, and source provenance are insufficiently specified for replay.","Electric vehicles are worse for carbon monoxide and particulates in the printed table, but these adverse results are not enforced in the selected policy.","Pollution symbols, signs, badness weights, and normalization are ambiguous, so the aggregate objective is not dimensionally transparent.","All badness factors are set to one; consequently the claimed health layer is not a dose, exposure, or health-outcome model.","The price curve uses invented ten-times-at-maximum and 2.5-times-at-midpoint anchors because supply curves are unavailable.","The integrated source cost and total Cost formulas omit the coefficient i on the first term, causing a dimensional and algebraic defect.","The text defines current production as zero for the curve while the following table prints nonzero current production, leaving the decision variable ambiguous.","Cost in dollars is added to a dimensionless pollution value, while alpha's units and scaling are unspecified.","Nelder-Mead does not guarantee a global optimum, and the asserted agreement with the genetic algorithm is unsupported by runs or tolerances.","The demand constraint is printed with <=, which permits under-supply and can make the zero-addition solution feasible.","Variables are called added QBTU but are bounded by current production values, mixing levels and increments.","The claimed monotonic cost-alpha relation and feasible pockets are not demonstrated mathematically or numerically.","No multi-start strategy, stopping tolerance, constraint residual, or convergence history is reported.","The fossil-fuel-saved formula divides by an unexplained factor of 20, reducing the stated gallons by that factor.","A 2011 seed expenditure is added directly to a 2060 grid cost without discounting, inflation, or a common price year.","At alpha=200,000 and seed 0.10, the printed total 1.28032e11 should be on the e12 scale from its two addends.","The text calls 1% the best seed for alpha=200,000 although the corresponding table tests no seed below 5%; nearby prose says 5-10%.","At alpha=500,000 and seed 0.35, the printed 7.37245e12 does not equal the displayed seed and grid costs.","The selected five-source mix sums to 108.15 QBTU, and it is unclear whether values are levels or additions; it conflicts with stated bounds.","Conclusion increments exceed some 25% maximums and do not reconcile with the selected source table.","The 5-10% 'optimal' seed is driven by the smallest tested seeds and lacks a service, adoption-benefit, or emissions constraint.","No actual pollution or health outcome is reported for the chosen seed and energy mix.","The requested public-health and economic consequences are not fully delivered despite the conclusion's broad claim.","No model is calibrated on held-out data, uncertainty is not propagated, and no final policy is independently validated.","Cited values and derived series are not frozen in a machine-readable dataset, preventing exact replay."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 20 physical pages retain nonempty source text and 200-DPI rasters. Page 1 is the title page, page 2 is Contents, pages 3-19 contain the author analysis, and page 20 is References; the source has neither Summary nor Abstract.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"All pages were read in physical order. Coverage retains the clarification and attack plan, micro adoption models, zero-state seeding, profitability handoff, cellular automaton tradeoff, power-source coefficients, generation-cost optimizer, alpha interface, energy-mix cases, combined cost, and policy conclusion.","status":"pass","validator":"source_coverage_audit"},{"details":"Human style is captured through stakeholder-separated framing; a declared micro-to-macro attack plan; explicit replacement of unavailable global data; explained scope exclusions; model failure triggering seeding and subsid