old.","When every neighbor is inactive, trapped population is explicitly excluded, violating conservation.","Migration has no capacity, nonnegative-stock, symmetry, calibration, or simultaneous-flow safeguards.","The plume equation treats Q as concentration, omits source height and ground reflection, and restricts direct exposure to adjacent nodes.","Policy and emergency effects are only described as changes to factors; no intervention operator or event distribution is specified.","Averaging four lattice thresholds is not justified for the actual geographic adjacency graph.","The claim that TCNM is nearly a two-dimensional lattice is not checked with degree, planarity, or topology diagnostics.","The data-source table omits harmonized spatial resolution, temporal frequency, missingness, licensing, and join keys.","Gradient descent is named for BBN training without an objective, parameterization, constraints, or convergence rule.","All three policy outputs are admitted expected empirical curves rather than computed model runs.","Scenario-one prose and trajectories conflict on threshold timing and whether industry and agriculture stagnate.","Sensitivity analysis supplies no perturbation design, response metric, numerical result, or uncertainty interval.","Natural disasters are mostly excluded despite being acknowledged as indispensable in some regions.","The closeness formula increases with total path length although the prose interprets larger values as faster spread.","Betweenness and closeness-like scores are averaged equally without orientation, scale, or weight validation.","Critical nodes and links receive ranks but no criterion for being critical, as the authors themselves admit.","No executable code, frozen data, fitted parameters, software versions, random seeds, or machine-readable scenario output is supplied."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 21 pages retain text and 200-DPI rasters; title, Summary, Introduction, and Conclusion