ced with zero.","Appendix C fixes k=13 and does not demonstrate all twenty profile items.","Appendix C hard-codes ARMAX order and mixture parameters; a2 is unused.","ypred2, ypred3 and ypred4 add datafit(1,50), a likely cross-state implementation bug.","Repeated terminal values and cumulative reconstruction are not reconciled with equations 20-23.","Inverse baseline-score weights have no fairness or welfare derivation.","The seven-criterion profile score is narrowed to RC-linked criteria without a complete handoff derivation.","Selfish governors are assumed but utility, bargaining, participation and opt-out behavior are absent.","The aggregate RC-production balance omits imports, exports, storage, transmission, loss and timing.","Softening RC less-than-production can permit infeasible targets instead of modeling transfers explicitly.","Minimum gains of 10/20 percent and penalty 0.015 lack calibration and stakeholder elicitation.","Summary and memo target numbers differ materially from Table 7 optimized targets.","Table 7's 10^14 Btu scale, summary billion-Btu values and improvement baselines are not reconciled.","Figures 11-12 are constructed target substitutions, not validation of policy effects.","Action 1 infers governmental promotion of unrenewable energy from a renewable-import increase.","The 556-to-482422 increase is about 867-fold, requiring standardized fold/percent wording.","Actions omit cost, technology, permitting, grid, transmission, reliability, market and legal feasibility.","CA export is recommended without capacity, distance, price, loss, contract or authority constraints.","Sensitivity curves report visual movement without forecast-error or decision-stability metrics.","Table 10 compares objective values under different objective weights, which are not directly comparable.","The small reference set uses weakly transferred or non-domain sources, including Wikipedia.","Uncertainty is not propagated from data and component models into targets or actions.","Adoption, rebound, emissions, cost, equity, reliability, schedule, monitoring and reversal are absent.","The memo states history, forecasts and targets more firmly than the evidence chain warrants.","MATLAB appendices omit inputs, preprocessing, environment, deterministic instructions and tests."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 30 physical pages retain page records and 200-DPI rasters; Summary, Introduction, Tables 1-10, equations 1-24, two optimization programs, Figures 1-13, Conclusion, governor memorandum, and MATLAB appendices are bound.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"Pages 1-30 were read in physical order; the third-party watermark, blank page, Contents, formula/table/caption regions, References, and code remain excluded from positive prose, while the governor memorandum remains author prose and code remains implementation evidence.","status":"pass","validator":"source_coverage_audit"},{"details":"The audit retains horizon-specific method rejection, acronym architecture, taxonomy after compression, observation-to-challenge routing, value/tendency and constant/evolving splits, counterexample-triggered repair, outmoded-data boundary, increment/look-aside/horizon-decay repair, easy-baseline failure, paired optimization repair, principles-before-actions, heterogeneous state roles, mechanistic sensitivity, and memo categories.","status":"pass","validator":"human_style_learning_audit"},{"details":"225 source-anchored language units cover eight normalized chapters with occurrences, function, order, slots, variants, boundary, disposition, and anti-copy restrictions.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"All 225 reviewed author-prose units passed with zero source-fact leaks and zero full-clause matches; the repeated watermark is absent.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_anticopy.py"},{"details":"Eight chapter contracts preserve inputs, rhetorical job