-DATA-003","R-C-MOD-001","R-C-MOD-002","R-C-MOD-003","R-C-MOD-004","R-C-MOD-005","R-C-MOD-006","R-C-MOD-007","R-C-VER-001","R-C-VER-002","R-C-VER-003","R-C-RESULT-001","R-C-DEC-001","R-C-ECO-001","R-C-CAUS-001","R-C-VIZ-001","R-C-LANG-001","R-C-AI-001"]},"unresolved_added":["The repeated third-party Chinese shop watermark contaminates every page and must never be treated as author prose or contest evidence.","Internal page numbering is offset by one from physical PDF pages; all citations must use physical page identity consistently.","The reduction from 605 variables to eleven basic variables has no reproducible selection criterion, missingness profile, redundancy analysis or leakage audit.","High- versus low-missingness is not given a numeric threshold, so deletion and interpolation cannot be reproduced.","The interpolation family, function selection, boundary treatment and imputation uncertainty are not reported.","The source defines an abnormal value by a two-standard-deviation rule but then invokes a box plot, which normally uses a different IQR criterion.","Replacing an outlier by the mean of adjacent observations can erase real shocks and ignores seasonality, trend and measurement provenance.","The CRE/TFE taxonomy is inconsistent with the memo, which treats Arizona nuclear power as a cleaner renewable advantage although nuclear is not listed in the CRE definition.","`Cleaner renewable` merges low-pollution and renewable properties without addressing life-cycle emissions, nuclear status or biomass sustainability.","The weighted average price formula does not define source-specific units, zero quantities or comparability across energy forms.","The eleven variables mix prices, expenditures, energy quantities, population and GDP without a common unit or normalization plan in the profile stage.","The assumption that all energy produced is consumed in the same state contradicts the interstate-trade setting and later cooperation narrative.","The unchanged-policy assumption through 2050 removes the main intervention mechanism the compact is supposed to create.","The constant-natural-environment assumption omits climate trends even though renewable potential and long-horizon planning are central.","`Mutual benefit` is repeatedly printed as `manual benefit`; source wording should not be learned as a reusable phrase.","Dual-axis profile plots can create visual correlation, yet scale choices and units are not standardized across panels or states.","Figure numbering and legend references are inconsistent: multiple appendix legends repeat earlier figure numbers and several captions use `constitute` or `cutline` incorrectly.","Table 4, presented as California, contains the same values later repeated for New Mexico in Table 16, including GDP 59,090; this is a major state-label/data duplication warning.","The appendix does not provide California source data separately enough to resolve whether Table 4 or Table 16 is mislabeled.","Arizona Table 14 reports GDP rate of change as `6.736912662` rather than a consistently formatted percentage, unlike the other rows.","The preliminary profile findings have no uncertainty, normalization sensitivity or formal cross-state test.","The elasticity formula uses an absolute value, removing direction even though decoupling usually distinguishes expansion, recession and sign regimes.","The paper calls the method decoupling analysis but never reports a decoupling-state taxonomy or thresholds.","Figure 4 offers dense time-series lines without a table of coefficients, uncertainty bands or reproducible source calculation.","The simultaneous-equations system gives no instruments, exclusion restrictions, estimator, identification check, sample size or diagnostics.","Natural-environment controls are removed for lack of data, so remaining coefficients can absorb omitted geography and climate effects.","Table 5 supplies coefficient stars but no standard errors, fit statistics, residual checks, endogeneity treatment or multiple-testing control.","The star legend calls 10%, 5% and 1% levels `confidence`, conflating significance levels and confidence.","The claim that population has no significant influence conflicts with starred New Mexico population coefficients in both TFE and CRE columns.","Regression association is described as `influence` or `impact` without a causal design.","The resource map provides qualitative context but is not integrated quantitatively into the simultaneous system after `X` is dropped.","Calling state strengths and weaknesses `congenital` risks treating policy and infrastructure outcomes as immutable natural endowments.","Several Table 6 symbols or meanings are unclear (`Pc`, `Tocs`, `Tpo`, `Csr/Cnr`), and notation differs from Table 1.","Development potential divides by lagged renewable production, which can be unstable near zero and can produce negative values without a stated direction rule.","The nine indicators mix benefit and cost directions, but the PCA pipeline does not state sign orientation before ranking.","If PCA is applied only to four states in 2009, nine indicators with four observations provide at most three nonzero components and make the score highly unstable.","Eigenvalues, eigenvectors, explained contribution rates and retained-component criteria are omitted, so equations 6-8 cannot reproduce Table 7.","PCA scores and the four-state ranking have no resampling, uncertainty, leave-one-indicator-out or comparison-set sensitivity.","CUP changes meaning: the evaluation CUP is a nine-indicator PCA score, the forecast CUP is first a three-indicator Cobb-Douglas form, and equation 10 then makes it linear.","The paper does not estimate or report `A`, `alpha`, `beta` or `gamma`, despite requiring their sum to equal one.","Carbon emissions per capita enters the multiplicative CUP without a clearly negative direction or transformation, so higher emissions can mechanically raise the score.","Equation 10's linear predictor relation is not reconciled with equation 9 or with the nonlinear BP network.","BP is selected because four forecasts are a heavy task and because it can approximate nonlinear functions, not because it outperforms a baseline.","Hidden-neuron count `k=9` is chosen without training/validation search, architecture rationale or complexity control.","Activation functions, learning rates, initialization, epochs, stopping rule, normalization and random seeds are not reported.","Equations 11-18 describe generic backpropagation but do not establish the actual trained network or reproducible parameter values.","Table 8 fitting errors and Table 10 prediction errors differ, but the source does not clearly separate training, fitting, validation and later-year testing.","Equation 19 is an average absolute error expression, while surrounding prose and tables use percentages; the scale conversion is not shown.","The 2010-2015 check does not state whether those years were excluded from training, how missing data were handled, or whether forecasts were produced recursively.","The paper refers to formula 15 for later prediction error even though equation 15 is the BP squared training loss, creating a formula-reference mismatch.","Future GDP, industry share and emissions paths are assumed through two scenarios; no probability, calibration, policy linkage or uncertainty band is supplied.","ARMA orders, coefficients, stationarity checks, residual diagnostics and selection criteria are absent.","Table 9 labels predictors `DPA`, `ROI` and `CEC`, while Section 5.4.1 names GDP per capita, `Sip` and `Cep`; predictor lineage is inconsistent.","Scenario CUP predictions have no intervals and no propagation of trajectory, parameter, preprocessing or model uncertainty.","Sensitivity perturbs only `k` by one or two neurons and calls the effect bearable without declaring an acceptance threshold.","At `k+2`, the mean deviation is 10.98% and Texas reaches 12.33%, which weakens the blanket claim that influence is not large.","Scenario two is selected because macroeconomies are `usually stable`, without checking the four state series or reporting scenario fit.","Cooperation is represented only by pooling four states into one economy; resource transfers, bargaining, transmission, incentives and participation are not modeled.","The cooperative CUP exceeds the independent average by only 0.86 in 2025 and 0.88 in 2050, with no uncertainty, cost or significance assessment.","`Maybe it is because cooperation` is a causal explanation inferred from an aggregation result, not identified evidence.","The compact goals include broad harmony and win-win language but no state-specific renewable-energy quantities, emissions caps, budgets or feasibility constraints.","The body lists four actions, the Summary promises three actions, and the memo provides three different recommendations; the stakeholder handoff is inconsistent.","Main-body actions are generic and are not each tied to a state, forecasted shortfall, quantified effect, cost, timing or monitoring threshold.","The memo's investment bank, public awareness and industrial adjustment recommendations are not the same as the body proposals on resource sharing, research, subsidies and periodic indicators.","The title promises a goal-setting system, but the final numeric goals are pooled CUP values whose definition changes across sections and whose unit is not stated.","The strengths claim accuracy and stability from limited fitting/later-year errors and a narrow `k` perturbation, without benchmark or probabilistic calibration.","The three source weaknesses are useful admissions but no correction, uncertainty bound or alternate result is supplied.","Omitting imports and exports is especially damaging because interstate exchange is the central policy mechanism of the requested compact.","The references concern renewable-energy policy and impacts but do not adequately document PCA, simultaneous equations, BP implementation or ARMA methodology.","The appendices contain only profile graphics/tables, no preprocessing code, model code, input files, environment, seeds or executable reproduction instructions.","No costs, reliability, grid capacity, storage, transmission losses, equity, legal authority, emissions trajectory or implementation schedule is modeled.","The memo presents ranking and future CUP targets without uncertainty or competing scenario values, making the decision language firmer than the evidence supports."],"unresolved_resolved":[],"validation_results":[{"details":"All 29 physical pages retain page records and 200-DPI rasters; Summary, Introduction, Tables 1-18, equations 1-21, BP flow, Figures 1-19, compact comparison, Conclusion, governor memorandum, and appendix profiles are bound.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_extraction.py"},{"details":"Pages 1-29 were read in physical order; the third-party watermark, Contents, formula/table/caption regions, References, and appendix graphics remain excluded from positive prose, while the governor memorandum and explicit Weaknesses remain author prose.","status":"pass","validator":"source_coverage_audit"},{"details":"The audit retains defect-sensitive routing, public compression and taxonomy, preliminary findings, question-triggered method switches, public control omission, bias-triggered evaluation, construct redefinition, missing-future-input scenarios, later-year checking, same-metric noncooperation baseline, pooled alternative, target-to-action order, explicit weaknesses, and memo categories.","status":"pass","validator":"human_style_learning_audit"},{"details":"201 source-anchored language units cover eight normalized chapters with occurrences, function, order, slots, variants, boundary, disposition, and anti-copy restrictions.","status":"pass","validator":"validate_language_units.py"},{"details":"All 201 reviewed author-prose units passed with zero source-fact leaks and zero full-clause matches; the repeated watermark is absent.","status":"pass